        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Export installed agents as grouped Claw packages",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add experimental `claws export <agent-id> --out <new-directory>`\n- project one installed agent into the grouped portable Claw schema\n- copy ledger-managed workspace files and safe workspace-relative avatars into package sidecars\n- always assign regenerated exports a derivative package identity and content-derived version\n- omit nonportable remote avatars, normalize empty optional arrays, and expand `~` in output paths\n\n## Scope\n\nExport reads the provenance established by the add/status lifecycle and writes a new self-contained package without mutating the installed Claw. It accepts an exact agent id, explicitly projects portable agent fields, copies only ledger-managed workspace files plus a validated local avatar, emits exact recorded package references, and refuses unavailable managed files or an existing output directory.\n\nImage data avatars remain inline. A safe local avatar is read through the pinned workspace avatar boundary, copied under `workspace/`, and rewritten to a workspace-relative manifest path. Remote, missing, or unsafe local avatars are omitted because they are not portable package state.\n\nEvery regenerated package is emitted as `openclaw-claw-<agent-id>@0.0.0-export.<content-hash>`, including an unchanged installation. Export never reuses an authenticated publisher's package name/version unless it can return the byte-for-byte original artifact, which this command intentionally does not do.\n\nThis slice emits the schema's JSON-compatible representation. The later dedicated #106888 slice changes the canonical exported representation to `CLAW.md` while preserving this package and round-trip behavior.\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102296 status/remove and ownership-aware lifecycle state\n- This PR: portable creation/export experience\n- Next: #102383 gateway-owned cron lifecycle\n- Canonical `CLAW.md`: #106888\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.test.src.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/test-src.tsbuildinfo`\n- Oxlint: 0 warnings, 0 errors across all 6 PR files\n- Oxfmt: all 6 PR files correctly formatted\n- 8 export unit tests\n- 15 Claws CLI tests\n- 8 full lifecycle E2E tests\n- `git diff --check`\n- Codex review: no accepted/actionable findings\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nThe real CLI E2E passes consent-bound add preview/apply -> export -> inspect -> consent-bound add preview/apply from the exported package in isolated state. Export writes `package.json`, `openclaw.claw.json`, managed workspace sidecars, and a portable agent manifest; the fresh add recreates the agent from the derivative package.\n",
